# Getting Started with AzureSDK

```elixir
Mix.install([
  # {:azure_sdk, path: Path.expand("..", __DIR__)},
  {:azure_sdk, "~> 0.3.0"},
])
```

## Overview

This notebook creates a Shared Key client against local Azurite, creates a container,
uploads a blob, and prints the blob name.

Requires Azurite:

```bash
docker compose up -d
```

Package version:

```elixir
AzureSDK.version()
```

## Create a client

Path-style endpoints (Azurite) are detected when the URL ends with the account name.

```elixir
credential =
  AzureSDK.Identity.SharedKeyCredential.new(
    "devstoreaccount1",
    "Eby8vdM02xNOcqFlqUwJPLlmEtlCDXJ1OUzFT50uSRZ6IFsuFq2UVErCz4I6tq/K1SZFPTOtr/KBHBeksoGMGw=="
  )

client =
  AzureSDK.Storage.Client.new(
    account: "devstoreaccount1",
    credential: credential,
    endpoint: "http://127.0.0.1:10000/devstoreaccount1"
  )

{client.endpoint, AzureSDK.Storage.Client.path_style?(client)}
```

## First upload

```elixir
container = "livebook-demo"

unless AzureSDK.Storage.Container.exists?(client, container) do
  {:ok, _} = AzureSDK.Storage.Container.create(client, container)
end

{:ok, blob} =
  AzureSDK.Storage.Blob.upload(client, container, "hello.txt", "Hello from Livebook!",
    content_type: "text/plain"
  )

blob.name
```

## Clean up

```elixir
{:ok, :deleted} = AzureSDK.Storage.Blob.delete(client, container, "hello.txt")
{:ok, :deleted} = AzureSDK.Storage.Container.delete(client, container)
:ok
```
